+# Phase 4.1: MuninnDB Integration — Context
+
+**Date:** 2026-03-05
+**Status:** Decisions locked, ready for planning
+
+## Current State
+
+- MuninnDB v0.3.6-alpha installed at `%LOCALAPPDATA%\muninn\muninn.exe`
+- Server running (pid 19692)
+- Ports: REST 8475, Web UI 8476, MCP 8750, MBP 8474, gRPC 8477
+- Default vault exists
+- Python SDK: `pip install muninndb` (not yet installed)
+- Brain MCP server: 12 tools, all Postgres-backed (`promaia/brain/mcp_server.py`)
+
+## Decisions
+
+### 1. Vault Architecture: Single Vault
+
+One vault for everything (`zbrain-vault`). No per-project vaults.
+
+**Rationale:** MuninnDB's Hebbian learning forms associations from co-retrieval. Splitting vaults kills cross-domain connections — the core value of cognitive memory. Decay handles noise (irrelevant stuff fades). Can split later if needed.
+
+**Implication:** All `capture` calls write to the same vault regardless of domain. Domain filtering happens at query time via tags, not vault separation.
+
+### 2. Retrieval Strategy: Parallel Trial
+
+Both pgvector search (Postgres) and ACTIVATE (MuninnDB) run during a 1-2 week trial period. Compare results side by side, then pick a primary with the other as backup.
+
+**Rationale:** MuninnDB is alpha software. Going all-in immediately risks losing retrieval if it breaks. Running both lets us evaluate quality with real usage data.
+
+**Implication:** The `search` MCP tool returns results from BOTH systems during trial, clearly labeled by source. After trial, switch to winner as primary with fallback to the other.
+
+### 3. MCP Tool Surface: Brain Wraps Everything
+
+Brain MCP server stays the single gateway to Claude. MuninnDB's own MCP server (port 8750) is NOT registered with Claude.
+
+**Rationale:** If Claude writes to MuninnDB directly AND through brain, memories desync. Wrapping through brain guarantees dual-write consistency and keeps the tool interface simple.
+
+**Implication:**
+- `capture` → modified to dual-write (Postgres + MuninnDB) internally
+- `search` → modified to query both systems during trial period
+- New tool: `activate` → MuninnDB cognitive retrieval (ACTIVATE pipeline)
+- No other new tools initially. 12 existing tools + 1 new = 13.
+
+### 4. Embedder & Enrichment: Gemini, No Enrichment
+
+Use Google Gemini embeddings (`MUNINN_GOOGLE_KEY`) matching the Postgres model (`gemini-embedding-001`). No LLM enrichment.
+
+**Rationale:** Consistent embeddings between systems. Hebbian learning builds the graph from usage patterns — that IS the cognitive feature. Paying for LLM enrichment on every write is redundant with existing `brain/extraction.py` and adds cost without clear value.
+
+**Implication:** Set `MUNINN_GOOGLE_KEY` env var on MuninnDB server. Do NOT set `MUNINN_ENRICH_URL`. Graph richness comes from usage, not preprocessing.
+
+## Implementation Scope
+
+### In Scope
+- Create `zbrain-vault` vault (public, no API key)
+- Configure Gemini embeddings on MuninnDB (`MUNINN_GOOGLE_KEY`)
+- Create `promaia/brain/muninn.py` — async httpx REST client (Python SDK broken on 3.14)
+- Modify `capture` tool for dual-write (Postgres + MuninnDB)
+- Modify `search` tool for parallel retrieval (both sources, labeled)
+- Add `activate` MCP tool (MuninnDB ACTIVATE pipeline)
+- Seed vault with existing `brain.memories` content via `writeBatch`
+- Verify MuninnDB Web UI accessible at localhost:8476
+
+### Out of Scope (Deferred)
+- MuninnDB MCP server registration with Claude
+- Multi-vault architecture
+- LLM enrichment
+- Replacing pgvector (decision deferred to after trial period)
+- MuninnDB as Windows service / auto-start (Phase 4.4 agent scheduler concern)
+
+## Key Files
+
+- `promaia/brain/mcp_server.py` — modify capture + search, add activate tool
+- `promaia/brain/muninn.py` — NEW: MuninnDB client wrapper
+- `promaia/brain/engine.py` — no changes expected
+- `.env` — add MUNINN_GOOGLE_KEY (same value as GOOGLE_API_KEY)
+
+## Dependencies
+
+- MuninnDB server must be running (manual start for now, auto-start deferred)
+- `pip install muninndb` — Python SDK
+- GOOGLE_API_KEY already configured for Gemini embeddings
+- Existing `brain.memories` data for seeding
